⍝ lib/list.imo — spec notation — trusted prelude, part 7: lists and streams, more Boolean connectives, digit-wise ("bitwise")
⍝ operations on the base i−1 representation, characters
⍝ ---- Booleans
⇒ ∶ 𝔹 → 𝔹 → 𝔹
⇒ ξ η ≔ (ξ η ⊤)
⇔ ∶ 𝔹 → 𝔹 → 𝔹
⇔ ξ η ≔ (ξ η (¬ η))
⍝ ---- lists (the head of an empty list is ⊥, i.e. false / 0-digit / nil)
hd ∶ 𝔏 α → α
hd ξ ≔ (ξ (η ζ ↦ η) ⊥)
foldr ∶ (α → β → β) → β → 𝔏 α → β
foldr ξ ζ η ≔ (η (θ ι ↦ (ξ θ (foldr ξ ζ ι))) ζ)
foldl ∶ (β → α → β) → β → 𝔏 α → β
foldl ξ ζ η ≔ (η (θ ι ↦ (foldl ξ (ξ ζ θ) ι)) ζ)
filter ∶ (α → 𝔹) → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
filter ξ η ≔ (η (θ ι ↦ ((ξ θ) (∷ θ (filter ξ ι)) (filter ξ ι))) ⊥)
take′ ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
take′ ν η ≔ ((∅ᶻ ν) ⊥ (η (θ ι ↦ (∷ θ (take′ (⊟ᶻ ν (◀ 1)) ι))) ⊥))
take ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
take ∶ ℕ → 𝔖 α → 𝔏 α
take ξ η ≔ (take′ (↓ᶻ ξ) η)
drop′ ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
drop′ ν η ≔ ((∅ᶻ ν) η (drop′ (⊟ᶻ ν (◀ 1)) (⌄ η)))
drop ∶ ℕ → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
drop ∶ ℕ → 𝔖 α → 𝔖 α
drop ξ η ≔ (drop′ (↓ᶻ ξ) η)
nth ∶ 𝔏 α → ℕ → α
nth ∶ 𝔖 α → ℕ → α
nth ξ η ≔ (hd (drop η ξ))
last ∶ 𝔏 α → α
last ξ ≔ (ξ (η ζ ↦ ((∅ ζ) η (last ζ))) ⊥)
reverse ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α
reverse ξ ≔ (foldl (η θ ↦ (∷ θ η)) ⊥ ξ)
concat ∶ 𝔏 (𝔏 α) → 𝔏 α
concat ξ ≔ (foldr ⧺ ⊥ ξ)
zip ∶ 𝔏 α → 𝔏 β → 𝔏 (𝔓 α β)
zip ξ η ≔ (⫴ ⊗ ξ η)
zipwith ∶ (α → β → γ) → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 β → 𝔏 γ
zipwith ∶ (α → β → γ) → 𝔖 α → 𝔖 β → 𝔖 γ
zipwith ≔ ⫴
replicate ∶ ℕ → α → 𝔏 α
replicate ξ η ≔ (take ξ (⁂ η))
iterate ∶ (α → α) → α → 𝔖 α
iterate ξ η ≔ (∷ η (iterate ξ (ξ η)))
⍝ the sequence f(0), f(1), f(2), …  as a stream (a real or complex number is such a sequence of approximants)
tabulate ∶ (ℕ → α) → 𝔖 α
tabulate ξ ≔ (⫶ ξ (iterate (η ↦ (⊞ η 1)) 0))
sumof ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ
sumof ∶ 𝔏 ℤ → ℤ
sumof ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → ℚ
sumof ∶ 𝔏 ℚ[i] → ℚ[i]
sumof ξ ≔ (foldl ⊞ 0 ξ)
prodof ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → ℕ
prodof ∶ 𝔏 ℤ → ℤ
prodof ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → ℚ
prodof ∶ 𝔏 ℚ[i] → ℚ[i]
prodof ξ ≔ (foldl ⊠ 1 ξ)
elem ∶ ℚ[i] → 𝔏 ℚ[i] → 𝔹
elem ξ η ≔ (∃ₗ (θ ↦ (≐ ξ θ)) η)
⍝ a, a + 1, …, b
upto ∶ ℕ → ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
upto ∶ ℤ → ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ
upto ξ η ≔ ((⩾ η ξ) (∷ ξ (upto (⊞ ξ 1) η)) ⊥)
⍝ insertion sort on ℚ, ascending and stable
ins′ ∶ ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ
ins′ ξ η ≔ (η (θ ι ↦ ((⩾ θ ξ) (∷ ξ η) (∷ θ (ins′ ξ ι)))) (∷ ξ ⊥))
sort ∶ 𝔏 ℕ → 𝔏 ℕ
sort ∶ 𝔏 ℤ → 𝔏 ℤ
sort ∶ 𝔏 ℚ → 𝔏 ℚ
sort ξ ≔ (foldr ins′ ⊥ ξ)
⍝ equality of lists, given an equality of elements;  equality of strings
eqlist ∶ (α → α → 𝔹) → 𝔏 α → 𝔏 α → 𝔹
eqlist ε ξ η ≔ (ξ (θ ι ↦ (η (θ′ ι′ ↦ (∧ (ε θ θ′) (eqlist ε ι ι′))) ⊥)) (∅ η))
≐ˢ ∶ 𝕊 → 𝕊 → 𝔹
≐ˢ ≔ (eqlist ≐)
⍝ ---- digit-wise operations on the base i−1 digits of Gaussian integers.  They are well defined on values because the expansion is
⍝ unique (trailing zeros give trailing zeros); they are what "bitwise and / or / xor" and "shifts" are in this number system.
∧ᵈ ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
∧ᵈ ξ η ≔ ((∨ (∅ ξ) (∅ η)) ⊥ (∷ (∧ (⌃ ξ) (⌃ η)) (∧ᵈ (⌄ ξ) (⌄ η))))
∨ᵈ ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
∨ᵈ ξ η ≔ ((∧ (∅ ξ) (∅ η)) ⊥ (∷ (∨ (⌃ ξ) (⌃ η)) (∨ᵈ (⌄ ξ) (⌄ η))))
⊻ᵈ ∶ 𝔇 → 𝔇 → 𝔇
⊻ᵈ ξ η ≔ ((∧ (∅ ξ) (∅ η)) ⊥ (∷ (⊻ (⌃ ξ) (⌃ η)) (⊻ᵈ (⌄ ξ) (⌄ η))))
band ∶ ℤ[i] → ℤ[i] → ℤ[i]
band ξ η ≔ (⊗ (⊡ (∧ᵈ (↓ᶻ ξ) (↓ᶻ η))) (◀ 1))
bor ∶ ℤ[i] → ℤ[i] → ℤ[i]
bor ξ η ≔ (⊗ (∨ᵈ (↓ᶻ ξ) (↓ᶻ η)) (◀ 1))
bxor ∶ ℤ[i] → ℤ[i] → ℤ[i]
bxor ξ η ≔ (⊗ (⊡ (⊻ᵈ (↓ᶻ ξ) (↓ᶻ η))) (◀ 1))
⍝ shifts: z·bⁿ (prepend n zeros) and the inverse that drops the n lowest digits
shl ∶ ℤ[i] → ℕ → ℤ[i]
shl ξ η ≔ (⊗ (⧺ (take η (⁂ ⊥)) (↓ᶻ ξ)) (◀ 1))
shr ∶ ℤ[i] → ℕ → ℤ[i]
shr ξ η ≔ (⊗ (drop η (↓ᶻ ξ)) (◀ 1))
⍝ number of digits of the expansion, and the digit at a position
ndigits ∶ ℤ[i] → ℕ
ndigits ξ ≔ (ℓ (⊡ (↓ᶻ ξ)))
digit ∶ ℤ[i] → ℕ → 𝔹
digit ξ η ≔ (nth (↓ᶻ ξ) η)
⍝ ---- characters.  𝕔 n is the character with code point n, unchecked: it is how the binary notation writes a Char literal
⍝ ('λ' is (𝕔 1110100000001000011001101)), so that a literal keeps its class 𝕮 in bin as in spec and hum
𝕔 ∶ ℕ → 𝕮
𝕔 ξ ≔ ξ
⍝ chr is total — a number that is not a Unicode scalar value (above U+10FFFF, or a surrogate) gives U+FFFD
chr ∶ ℕ → 𝕮
chr ξ ≔ ((∧ (⩽ ξ 10000000100000000000000000000000000011101) (¬ (∧ (⩾ ξ 100011100110000000000000000000000) (⩽ ξ 100011100000000000000000000011101)))) ξ 100000000000000000000000000010001)
